ollection","title":"Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/joined(by:)-3vukc":{"conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"joined"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"by"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"JoinedBySequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms16JoinedBySequenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s15CollectionOfOneV","text":"CollectionOfOne","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">>","kind":"text"}],"title":"joined(by:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/joined(by:)-3vukc","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/joined(by:)-3vukc","abstract":[],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]}}}